          {
            "id": "p40-q5-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Subtract the two excluded triangles from the square of possible pairs.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let the two numbers be $u,v\\in[0,10]$. Their possible pairs fill a square of area $100$. We require $|u-v|\\le2$, the region between $v=u-2$ and $v=u+2$. The excluded regions are two right triangles, each with perpendicular sides of length $8$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\nA_{\\text{excluded}}&=2\\left(\\frac12\\times8\\times8\\right)\\\\\nA_{\\text{excluded}}&=64\\\\\n\\Pr(|u-v|\\le2)&=\\frac{100-64}{100}\\\\\n\\Pr(|u-v|\\le2)&=\\frac{9}{25}\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 48
  },
